    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><dateline><date when="1948-05-15">May 15, 1948</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4553" type="person">Miss
                        Krauss</rs>:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Prof. Tillich</rs>, before his
                    departure to <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__122" type="place">Germany</rs>, asked
                    me to write to you on behalf of <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__5092" type="person"
                        >Dr. Anita Orienter</rs>.</p>
                <p><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__5092" type="person">Dr. Orienter</rs> has come to
                    the <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__684" type="place">U. S.</rs> about two weeks
                    ago. She seeks a teaching position for fall, but also some work during the
                    summer. Her problem is that she is not alone but that she has to take care of
                        <rs type="person">her mother</rs> who is about 70 years old – healthy and
                    active. It was my idea that <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__5092" type="person">Dr.
                        Orienter</rs> may work in a camp as a teacher (She has taught French and
                    Spanish for many years in <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__1540" type="place"
                        >Brazil</rs>) without renumeration and may take her mother along for the two
                    summer months. But I do not know wether this is feasible.</p>
                <p>I should be grateful for any advices you may give <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__5092" type="person">Dr. Orienter</rs>. Is there a
                    chance that you come to <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New
                        York</rs> in the near future? Or is there somebody of the American Friends
                    Service Committee whom <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__5092" type="person">Dr.
                        Orienter</rs> could see in <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New
                        York</rs>? May I mention that <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__5092"
                        type="person">Dr. Orienter</rs> is Catholic.</p>
                <p>I would suggest that you contact <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__5092" type="person"
                        >Dr. Orienter</rs> directly. Her address is: Hotel Paris, West End Avenue
                    and 97 St<supplied>,</supplied>
                    <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York</rs>, <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__865" type="place">N. Y.</rs></p>
                <closer>
                    <salute>With every good wish,<lb/>Sincerely yours,</salute>
                    <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4907" type="person">Secretary to Prof.
                            Tillich</rs></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
